  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nHigh pressure gradually shifts south of New England through the\nday today following a cool start to the day. As the high \ncontinues to move southward, a moderating southwest flow brings \nwarmer temps by the end of the weekend. Temps rebound back into \nthe 60s for Sunday and Monday, with some low 70s also possible \non Monday.\n\nA weak front passes through on Monday with just a few sprinkles\nacross the north. Behind the front, a new high pressure center \narrives with a cooler airmass. Highs return to the 40s and 50s \nfor Tuesday and Wednesday, before beginning to rebound back into\nthe 60s for the end of the week as the high moves offshore. \nAnother weak front is possible by the end of the week, but looks\nmostly dry at this point.",
